course: dictionary
lesson: 1296
title: Bye: goodbye and more
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Bye is a short, friendly way to say goodbye. «Bye for now» means you are leaving, but you will see the person again soon. Context tells you which meaning you need.
explain: Bye also has special meanings in sport. If a team goes on to the next round without playing because it has no opponent, that is a bye. In cricket, a bye is a run scored when the ball passes the batter without being hit. Look at the words around bye to work out which meaning fits.
explain: Buy, by and bye sound the same but are spelled differently and mean different things. «Buy» means pay for, «by» means near or through, and «bye» means goodbye. Always check the spelling and the sentence before you choose.
fact: Bye is an interjection when you say it on its own, as in «Bye!».
fact: «Bye-bye» is often said to small children when they leave.
fact: A bye (noun) in sport means a team goes to the next round without playing, because there is no opponent.
fact: In cricket, a bye is a run scored when the ball passes the batter without being hit.
fact: Buy, by and bye sound the same but mean different things.
exercise: Which spelling means goodbye: buy, by or bye? | buy | by | *bye
exercise: In a sports competition, a team goes on to the next round without playing because it has no opponent. What is this called? | a goal | *a bye | a run | a wicket
exercise: «Say Hi for 2 seconds», «wait 1 seconds», «say Bye for 2 seconds» takes how many seconds in total? | 6 | 4 | 3 | *5
test: In cricket, when does a bye score a run? | when the batter hits a six | *when the ball passes the batter without being hit | when the bowler takes a wicket
test: Which phrase uses a different word, not bye? | bye for now | say bye | *by the way | bye-bye
exam: In «Buy» means pay for, «by» means near, «bye» means goodbye, which spelling means goodbye? | by | bey | *bye | buy
